      "A 36-year-old with an IQ of 69 has managed a newspaper delivery route independently for seven years — planning their own schedule, collecting payment from customers, and liaising with the distributor about supply issues. They recently expanded the route by ten customers through their own initiative. They drive their own car, hold a standard license, and manage their household finances without assistance. They attend a weekly community group and serve as an informal mentor to younger members. Their functioning in all of these domains is indistinguishable from that of someone with an IQ of 75 or 80 — the score boundary is irrelevant to their daily life.",
