      "An IQ of 76 is in the borderline range — four points below low average. The functional profile here is substantially similar to that of IQ 80, with reading, arithmetic, communication, and practical reasoning all adequate for most real-world tasks. Reading comprehension is typically at a fifth- to sixth-grade level; practical math covers the arithmetic operations needed for work and daily finance. The individual navigates complex social environments, interprets unwritten rules in workplaces and communities, and manages personal relationships with skill. Abstract and formal reasoning is below average, which constrains performance in academic contexts and complex analytical tasks. In practical, structured environments with clear goals and concrete feedback, performance is solid and often indistinguishable from that of individuals with significantly higher IQs.",
