      "An IQ of 88 is at the upper boundary of the low average range — twelve points below the mean, within the range that will sometimes be described as simply 'below average' rather than the more specific 'low average' classification. Cognitive abilities at this level are broadly functional for most tasks in modern daily and occupational life. Reading comprehension at a ninth- to tenth-grade level, arithmetic through introductory algebra, written communication for most professional purposes including formal correspondence and reports, and verbal reasoning adequate for sophisticated discussions in familiar domains are all well established. Abstract reasoning is the primary area of limitation — formal symbolic reasoning, advanced inferential comprehension, and complex theoretical analysis are challenging. In applied, concrete, and interpersonal domains, performance at this level is often indistinguishable from that of individuals with average IQs.",
